# Witness: an approval attested with a hyphen in every field

None of these values is empty, none is italicised, and none is one of the placeholder words. A
closed word list cannot enumerate every way of writing nothing, so a value carrying no letter
and no digit is refused on its own terms - an approval whose four attestation fields all read
"-" is precisely the outcome this rule exists to refuse.

## 9. Decision

- [x] **APPROVED FOR PREVIEW** within the intended-use scope above.
- [ ] **APPROVED WITH CONDITIONS** listed below.
- [ ] **NOT APPROVED.**
- [ ] **PENDING** - not yet reviewed.

